++### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs (Project Settings)
++
++- **name:** The project name displayed across navigation breadcrumbs, issue peek drawers, and workspace summary cards. Scoped strictly to the active workspace (max 120 characters).
++- **key:** The immutable uppercase prefix key identifying work items within this project (e.g. `KAN` generates `KAN-1`, `KAN-2`). Validated against `^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]{1,9}$` (between 2 and 10 alphanumeric characters).
++- **state_name:** The human-facing title of a workflow state (e.g. `Backlog`, `In Progress`, `Code Review`, `Done`). Renaming a state immediately reflects across all active cards without modifying historical audit events.
++- **group:** The canonical lifecycle category to which the state belongs (`backlog`, `unstarted`, `started`, `completed`, `cancelled`). Group mapping is fundamental: cycle burndowns, cumulative flow diagrams, and throughput percentiles aggregate work based on group identity.
++- **color_hex:** A 7-character hexadecimal color string (`#RRGGBB`) applied to column lane headers, state pills, and board drop zones to ensure high contrast and immediate readability.
++- **sort_order:** An integer specifying the left-to-right presentation order of board columns and workflow dropdowns. Lower numbers appear earlier in the delivery lifecycle.
++- **is_default:** Designates the initial workflow state automatically assigned when a contributor quick-creates an issue without specifying a state. Exactly one state per project can be default.
++- **wip_soft_limit:** An advisory Work-In-Progress limit for Kanban columns (1 to 999). When the active card count exceeds this number, the column header displays an amber count badge (`5/4 WIP`) without preventing drops.
++- **wip_hard_limit:** A strict Work-In-Progress enforcement threshold (1 to 999). When reached, further card drops or status changes targeting this column are rejected at the API boundary (`422 WIP_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`). Must be greater than or equal to `wip_soft_limit`.
++- **priority_slug:** Machine-readable identifier for priority tiers (`urgent`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `none`). Used in Safe Formula evaluations, MCP tool queries, and REST search filters.
++- **priority_label:** The user-facing priority string, typically combining an expressive semantic emoji and clear text (e.g. `🔴 Urgent`, `🟠 High`, `🟡 Medium`, `🔵 Low`).
++- **exclusive_group:** An optional label category constraint. When applied to tags (e.g. `tier:free`, `tier:pro`), applying one tag from the group automatically removes any previously attached tags in that same exclusive group.
